Brother DCP-T300 Void Linux packaging repository
Copyright (C) 2026 the repository contributors

This repository contains packaging recipes to build the Brother DCP-T300
printer driver for Void Linux. It is NOT a single-work project: different
parts are licensed differently.

1. Packaging files (srcpkgs/*/template)
   ------------------------------------
   The xbps-src build templates are plain shell scripts describing how to
   fetch, build and package upstream software. They are provided under the
   terms of the Creative Commons Zero (CC0 1.0) license, or, at your option,
   the ISC license. No warranty of any kind is provided.

   <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/>
   <https://opensource.org/license/isc-license>

2. Static CUPS wrapper (srcpkgs/brother-dcpt300-cupswrapper/files/...)
   -------------------------------------------------------------------
   The static CUPS filter wrapper `brother_lpdwrapper_dcpt300` is derived
   from the upstream Brother `cupswrapperdcpt300` script, whose package
   metadata declares "Copyright: GPL". The wrapper is therefore licensed
   under the GNU General Public License, version 2 or (at your option) any
   later version, as published by the Free Software Foundation.

   <https://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/gpl-2.0.txt>

3. Proprietary Brother binaries
   ----------------------------
   The actual printer driver binaries (brdcpt300filter, brcupsconfpt1,
   brprintconf_dcpt300, filters, firmware/LUT data files and the PPD) are
   proprietary software owned by Brother Industries, Ltd. They are NOT
   distributed from this repository and are NOT covered by the licenses
   above.

   They are downloaded automatically at build time from the official
   Brother download server using the `distfiles` and `checksum` declared in
   the build templates, and are used under Brother's own license terms.

4. No redistribution rights
   ------------------------
   This repository does not grant any right to redistribute the proprietary
   Brother binaries. Redistribution of those binaries is governed solely by
   Brother Industries, Ltd. and must be performed in accordance with their
   terms.

By using this repository you accept that you are responsible for complying
with the license terms of every component you build and install.
